<title>USA: Dodge City feeder steer prices mixed - USDA.</title>
<headline>Dodge City feeder steer prices mixed - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DODGE CITY 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Feeder steers and heifers 300-600 lbs in a limited supply weak to $3.00 per cwt lower; 600-1000 lbs firm to $1.00 higher, compared with last week, USDA said.</p>
<p>Trade moderate, demand good. Receipts 72 percent 600 lbs and over; 21 percent 600 lbs and under; 07 percent cows and bulls with 200 early.</p>
<p>Feeder Steers - (Figures in parentheses are weighted</p>
<p>average prices) Medium and Large 1 600-650 lbs 80.50-85.50</p>
<p>(84.55); 650-700 lbs 80.50-83.85 (81.61); 700-750 lbs</p>
<p>78.10-83.75 (79.96); 750-800 lbs 75.85-79.00 (77.87); 800-850</p>
<p>lbs 75.00-80.00 (77.48); 850-900 lbs 74.50-78.60 (76.00);</p>
<p>900-950 lbs 73.75-74.20 (74.09); 950-1000 lbs 72.50-73.75</p>
<p>(73.09).</p>
<p>Feeder Heifers Medium and Large 1 600-650 lbs 76.50-78.25</p>
<p>(76.99); 650-700 lbs 74.00-77.50 (75.18); 700-750 lbs</p>
<p>73.75-76.10 (74.67); 750-800 lbs 72.75-75.35 (74.47); 800-850</p>
<p>lbs 73.00-74.00 (73.32); 35 head 857 lbs 69.50. Medium and</p>
<p>Large 1-2 550- 600 lbs 74.00-80.00 (77.21); 14 head 706 lbs</p>
<p>71.75; 22 head 750 lbs 72.75; 800-850 lbs 69.75-70.50 (70.09).</p>
<p>Receipts - 2,999   Last Week - 3,557   Last Year - 3,255</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
